Patch T12 oracles (rung 1b, task T12; gates G5 and G6): protect the shot
harness, and propose its FLIP thresholds.

- crates/game-testbed/tests/shots.rs and its modules in
  crates/game-testbed/tests/shots/ (`compare.rs`, the comparison, and
  `parts.rs`, its GPU-free tests; `#[path]` modules, so a pattern of their
  own) join protected.toml and .github/CODEOWNERS (proposal 8, the G5 row
  "Protect the new harnesses: `shots.rs`, ..."; criteria 4 `shot-exact`
  and 5 `shot-flip`). The lines sit right after `**/golden/**`, so this
  applies in any order with the queued patches that add lines after
  `known_answers.rs`, `version.rs` and `shaders.rs`.
- crates/game-testbed/golden/thresholds.toml, the FLIP limits off the
  pinned configuration: the plan's proposed values (G6 row: mean at most
  0.01, 99th percentile at most 0.2) and a third, the 99.9th percentile at
  most 0.5, without which a missing dot passes (mean 0.007, p99 0.10,
  p999 0.98). Before any golden exists the harness reports "no golden yet"
  with or without this file, so it can land at G5 or wait for G6 with the
  golden images.

Base: main with T12's commit, which adds the harness. At the repo root,
run `git apply` with this file, then `cargo xtask quick`.
Session 17's T12 entry in PROGRESS.md says how it was tested.
Text before the first `diff --git` line is ignored by `git apply`.

